# CORE PRINCIPLE

> Architecture is the source of truth for system design.

No feature, refactor, or AI-generated change may violate architectural boundaries.

---

# 1. SYSTEM OVERVIEW

AI-Investor is a:

> AI-native financial dashboard + QA engineering reference platform

It demonstrates:
- modern frontend architecture (Next.js + React)
- service-oriented backend abstraction
- AI-assisted engineering workflows
- production-grade QA automation practices

---

# 2. ARCHITECTURAL STYLE

The system follows a:

> Layered Modular Architecture with Service + Provider separation

NOT a monolith of UI logic.

---

# 3. LAYERED ARCHITECTURE MODEL

## 3.1 UI LAYER (React / Next.js)

Responsibilities:
- rendering UI components
- handling user interactions
- managing local UI state only
- invoking service layer

FORBIDDEN:
- direct API calls (fetch/axios)
- business logic
- data transformation logic (beyond UI formatting)

---

## 3.2 SERVICE LAYER (Business Logic)

Location:
- `/services/*`

Responsibilities:
- business logic
- orchestration of data
- transformation logic
- validation rules (non-security critical)

RULE:
All domain logic MUST live here.

---

## 3.3 PROVIDER LAYER (External Integration)

Location:
- `/providers/*`

Responsibilities:
- external API calls (Yahoo Finance, etc.)
- third-party integration logic
- request/response normalization

RULE:
Providers must NOT contain business logic.

---

## 3.4 API LAYER (Next.js Routes)

Location:
- `/app/api/*`

Responsibilities:
- request handling
- authentication checks (if applicable)
- calling service layer
- returning standardized responses

RULE:
API routes must be thin controllers ONLY.

---

## 3.5 DATA LAYER (Persistence)

Responsibilities:
- database access (if applicable)
- schema definitions
- data integrity

RULE:
No business logic allowed in data layer.

---

## 3.6 AI LAYER

Location:
- `/docs/ai/`
- `/agents/` (if introduced)

Responsibilities:
- AI-assisted workflows
- prompt definitions
- structured AI outputs
- automation tools (test generation, analysis)

RULE:
AI must never directly modify system state without validation.

